<title>USA: FP&amp;L Turkey Pt 4 nuke cut to 40 pct output.</title>
<headline>FP&amp;L Turkey Pt 4 nuke cut to 40 pct output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power and Light Co's 666 megawatt (MW) Turkey Point 4 nuclear power unit has been reduced to 40 percent output for maintenance, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>The NRC's morning plant status report stated that the unit, in Florida City, Fla., was reduced for &quot;condenser waterbox cleaning and other maintenance.&quot;</p>
<p>The adjacent 666 MW unit, Turkey Point 3, has resumed full power operation after being cut to 55 percent output last week.</p>
<p>Florida Power is a subsidiary of the FPL Group.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
